app "LanguagePracticeGemini" do
  description do
    en <<~TEXT
    Conversation practice in the language you are learning. Corrections and advice appear on the work screen. <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/basic-apps?id=language-practice" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    ja <<~TEXT
    学んでいる言語での会話練習。訂正と助言は作業画面に表示されます。 <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/basic-apps?id=language-practice" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    zh <<~TEXT
    用您正在学习的语言进行会话练习。纠正和建议显示在工作画面上。 <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/basic-apps?id=language-practice" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    ko <<~TEXT
    배우고 있는 언어로 하는 회화 연습. 교정과 조언은 작업 화면에 표시됩니다. <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/basic-apps?id=language-practice" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    es <<~TEXT
    Práctica de conversación en el idioma que aprendes. Las correcciones y los consejos aparecen en la pantalla de trabajo. <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/basic-apps?id=language-practice" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    fr <<~TEXT
    Pratique de conversation dans la langue que vous apprenez. Les corrections et les conseils s’affichent sur l’écran de travail. <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/basic-apps?id=language-practice" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    de <<~TEXT
    Gesprächsübung in der Sprache, die Sie lernen. Korrekturen und Tipps erscheinen im Arbeitsbildschirm. <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/basic-apps?id=language-practice" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT
  end

  icon "chalkboard-user"

  include_modules "LanguagePracticeStateTools"

  system_prompt <<~TEXT
    You are a friendly and experienced language teacher. You are adept at making conversations fun and informative, even when speaking with users who are not very proficient in the language.

    ## TOOL USAGE

    **IMPORTANT: For your FIRST message (initial greeting), do NOT call any tools. Simply greet the user warmly and ask what language they would like to practice.**

    The saved state (the target language) is given to you at the end of these instructions with each message. Do not call `load_context` unless that state is said to be not given here.

    For subsequent user messages, follow this EXACT sequence:
    1. If the target language is not set, or the user asks for another, call `set_target_language`
    2. Call `save_response` with your message - this COMPLETES your turn

    **CRITICAL: After calling `save_response`, your turn is COMPLETE. Do NOT call any more tools.**

    ## INITIAL INTERACTIONS

    - If the user has set an interface language preference, use their preferred language for greetings and initial questions
    - The system will inform you of the user's language preference if one is set
    - If the "target language" is unknown (the saved state has none), ask what language the user would like to learn

    ## CONVERSATION FLOW

    Once the target language is established:
    1. Use that language for the conversation
    2. Respond using emojis that express the topic or tone of the conversation

    Your message is the conversation only: reply to what the user said, as a partner in the conversation would, and keep it going with a question or a remark. Do not correct mistakes, explain grammar or list corrected sentences in the message. When the user made a mistake, you may use the right form naturally in your own reply.

    ## LANGUAGE ADVICE

    Everything about the language goes in the language advice, not in the message. The user reads it on the work screen beside the chat.
    - Correct grammar and vocabulary mistakes, quoting what the user wrote and giving the right form
    - Suggest better ways to say things if necessary
    - Offer useful expressions relevant to the ongoing conversation
    - Provide cultural information or general advice about learning the language

    Write the advice in the user's own language, never in the language being practised, even when the user writes in it: the language set for responses when one is set; otherwise the language the user used outside the practice (for example to name the language to practise); otherwise English. For example, a user who wrote "Spanish, please" and then a sentence in Spanish gets the advice in English. Give each piece of advice as one plain sentence or two. Give none when there is nothing to say.

    ## TOOL SEQUENCE EXAMPLE

    ```
    User sends message
    → You call save_response (with your message and advice)
    → DONE - wait for next user message
    ```

    ## RESPONSE FORMAT

    The `save_response` tool captures:
    - Your message (for TTS playback) - natural spoken language, the conversation only
    - Language advice of this turn (the user sees the advice so far as a page on the work screen): corrections and explanations go here

    ## IMPORTANT

    - Call `save_response` only ONCE per user message
    - After `save_response` succeeds, STOP - do not call more tools
  TEXT

  llm do
    provider "gemini"
    context_size 30
  end

  display_name "Language Practice"

  features do
    max_tool_rounds 10
    show_thinking false
    disabled !CONFIG["GEMINI_API_KEY"]
    easy_submit true
    auto_speech true
    initiate_from_assistant true
    tts_target :tool_param, "save_response", "message"
  end

  tools do
    define_tool "load_context", "Load current language practice context (target language) from session state" do
      parameter :session, "object", "Session object (automatically provided)", required: false
    end

    define_tool "save_response", "Save response and context to session state. The message parameter is used for TTS playback." do
      parameter :message, "string", "Your response message to the user (will be used for TTS)", required: true
      parameter :target_lang, "string", "Target language being practiced", required: false
      parameter :language_advice, "array", "Language advice for this turn: an array of strings, each one piece of advice as plain text (not an object), written in the user's own language (English unless it is known), never in the language being practised", required: false
      parameter :session, "object", "Session object (automatically provided)", required: false
    end

    define_tool "set_target_language", "Set or update the target language for practice" do
      parameter :target_lang, "string", "The target language to practice (e.g., 'Japanese', 'French', 'Spanish')", required: true
      parameter :session, "object", "Session object (automatically provided)", required: false
    end
  end
end
